<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-lgdel.l2 (epic nexus-lgdel, T2 nexus/plan-legacy-retirement-2026-08-16)
    — DROP the orphaned nexus.remap_membership(text, text) read surface.

    ORPHAN CENSUS (bead nexus-lgdel.l2, item 2): live SQL and Java, ZERO
    production Python/CLI callers. The old client's membership-reading rung
    was deleted at 88d91bd58; the surviving upgrade-ladder rung calls only
    POST /v1/remap/rekey. This is the largest remaining orphan the L2 sweep
    found — and it is exactly the function L1's legacy-001-4 changeset spent
    a changeset simplifying (removing the chash_alias LEFT JOIN) one commit
    before it turns out to have no callers at all.

    RELAY ASK (Hal-relayed, non-blocking, per the plan of record): "does any
    managed or external deployment call GET /v1/remap/membership?" The
    default disposition is DELETE regardless of the answer — under the
    epic's directive of record the canary-class gates are the backstop for
    an undiscovered caller, not a blocking census. RemapHandler's own class
    javadoc already notes its edge carries no path allowlist, so this is the
    accepted risk, not an oversight.

    NOT IN SCOPE (PERMANENT BY DESIGN, RDR-194 D3, unchanged by this file):
    nexus.chash_remap the TABLE, and RemapHandler's record_batch/clear_leg
    WRITE surface. Only the read (membership) is deleted here.

    ONE CHANGESET: DROP FUNCTION nexus.remap_membership(text, text).
    Rollback restores the exact L1-generation body (legacy-001-4's forward
    body — the alias-join-free form; chash_alias itself does not exist by
    the time ANY of this file's forward or rollback SQL runs, so restoring
    the pre-L1 alias-joined body here would be a straight typecheck failure,
    not merely dishonest like legacy-001-5's EMPTY-table recreation). Safe
    unconditionally: the function references only nexus.chash_remap and
    nexus.chunks, both of which exist for the lifetime of this changeset in
    both directions.

    Tail-appended after legacy-001-drop-chash-alias.xml (current tail) and
    before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, matching the
    established late-append convention (D0.1; see catalog-031's /
    telemetry-004's / aspects-003's / plans-002's / taxonomy-008's /
    catalog-032's / remap-003's / taxonomy-009's / legacy-001's own
    <include> comments for the identical reasoning).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset 1: DROP FUNCTION nexus.remap_membership(text, text) ──── -->
    <changeSet id="legacy-002-1" author="nexus-lgdel.l2">
        <comment>
            DROP the orphaned nexus.remap_membership(text, text) read
            surface — zero production Python/CLI callers (the old client's
            membership-reading rung was deleted at 88d91bd58; the surviving
            rung calls only POST /v1/remap/rekey). Java-side deletion
            (RemapHandler.handleMembership, the GET /v1/remap/membership
            route, RemapRepository.membership) lands in the same commit
            family. nexus.chash_remap the TABLE and the record_batch/
            clear_leg write surface are UNTOUCHED (RDR-194 D3, permanent
            by design).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
DROP FUNCTION nexus.remap_membership(text, text);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <!-- Restores the exact L1-generation body (legacy-001-4's
                 forward body — the alias-join-free form). This is the
                 correct restoration target, NOT the pre-L1 alias-joined
                 form: nexus.chash_alias does not exist at this changeset's
                 position in the reverse walk (legacy-001-5's own rollback,
                 which recreates it, runs LATER in reverse order — legacy-001
                 is entirely BEFORE legacy-002 in forward order, so its
                 rollback entirely FOLLOWS legacy-002's in reverse order) —
                 restoring an alias-joined body here would reference a
                 table that does not exist yet, a straight typecheck
                 failure. Signature and return contract (RETURNS TABLE
                 (mapped_total bigint, present_count bigint), SECURITY
                 INVOKER, STABLE) unchanged from L1's. -->
            <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION nexus.remap_membership(
    p_source_collection text,
    p_target_collection text
) RETURNS TABLE(mapped_total bigint, present_count bigint)
LANGUAGE sql
STABLE
SECURITY INVOKER
AS $fn$
    SELECT
        count(*)::bigint AS mapped_total,
        count(*) FILTER (WHERE
            EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM nexus.chunks c
                     WHERE c.collection = p_target_collection
                       AND c.chash = r.new_chash)
        )::bigint AS present_count
    FROM nexus.chash_remap r
    WHERE r.source_collection = p_source_collection
      AND r.target_collection = p_target_collection
$fn$;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION nexus.remap_membership(text, text) TO nexus_svc;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
